@	
s	commands	List all available JEnv commands
s	help	Parses and displays help contents from a command's source file
s	info	Show information about which command will be executed
s	add	Add JDK into jenv. A alias name will be generated by parsing "java -version"
s	enable-plugin	Activate a jEnv plugin
s	disable-plugin	Deactivate a jEnv plugin
s	doctor	Run jEnv diagnostics
s	exec	Runs an executable by first preparing PATH so that the selected Java version's `bin' directory is…
s	global	Sets the global Java version
s	global-options	Sets the global Java options
s	local	Sets the local application-specific Java version by writing the version name to a file named…
s	local-options	Sets the local application-specific Java options
s	shell	Sets a shell-specific Java version by setting the `JENV_VERSION'
s	shell-options	Sets the shell-specific Java options
s	hooks	List hook scripts for a given jenv command
s	init	Configure the shell environment for jenv
s	javahome	Display path to selected JAVA_HOME
s	macos-javahome	Installs a file located at ~/Library/LaunchAgents/jenv-environment.plist . It sets JAVA_HOME for…
s	options	Show the current Java options
s	options-file	Detect the file that sets the current jenv jvm options
s	options-file-read	Read options from file
s	options-file-write	Write options to a file
s	prefix	Displays the directory where a Java version is installed
s	refresh-plugins	Refresh plugins links
s	refresh-versions	Refresh alias names
s	rehash	Rehash jenv shims (run this after installing executables)
s	remove	Remove JDK installations
s	root	Display the root directory where versions and shims are kept
s	shims	List existing jenv shims
s	version	Shows the currently selected Java version and how it was selected
s	versions	Lists all Java versions found in `$JENV_ROOT/versions/*'
s	whence	List all Java versions that contain the given executable
s	which	Displays the full path to the executable that jenv will invoke when you run the given command
o	--help|-h	Show help for jEnv	
o	--version	Show version for jEnv	
